"Math layout regressions
'<p>Stress cases for equation layout. Each case is labelled so a screenshot can be matched back to its source line. <i>Math layout regressions MathML.cpd</i> renders this file with <code>#settings {"mathRenderer": "mathml"}</code> for comparison.</p>
#hide
a = 3
b = 4
c = 5
d = 2
p = 7
q = 6
n = 3
x = 0.5
y = 2
z = 1.5
σ_x = 1.2
γ_c = 1.5
f_ck = 30MPa
M = 45kN*m
b_w = 300mm
h = 500mm
q_d = 12kN/m^2
L = 6m
k_s = 2*m^(1/2)
#show
'<h3>A. Powers</h3>
'A1 power with fraction exponent in a denominator (#282)
A_1 = 1/1^(5/4)
'A2 same with variables
A_2 = a/b^(c/d)
'A3 raised power of a fraction
A_3 = (a/b)^(c/d)
'A4 raised power of a fraction, inside a denominator
A_4 = 1/(a/b)^(c/d)
'A5 power tower
A_5 = a^(b^(1/2))
'A6 Gaussian, fraction with power inside the exponent
A_6 = e^(-x^2/(2*σ_x^2))
'A7 nested fraction in exponent
A_7 = y^(1/(1 + 1/n))
'A8 square root in exponent
A_8 = y^sqrt(2)
'A9 n-th root in exponent
A_9 = y^root(a; 3)
'A10 bracketed fraction to a power
A_10 = (1 + 1/n)^n
'A11 bracketed fraction to a fractional power, inside a denominator
A_11 = 1/(1 + 1/n)^(n/2)
'A12 power of a power of a fraction
A_12 = ((a/b)^2)^(1/3)
'<h3>B. Fractions</h3>
'B1 continued fraction, three levels
B_1 = 1/(1 + 1/(1 + 1/x))
'B2 continued fraction, four levels (switches to ÷)
B_2 = 1/(1 + 1/(1 + 1/(1 + 1/x)))
'B3 fraction over fraction
B_3 = (a/b)/(c/d)
'B4 mixed fractions in numerator and denominator
B_4 = (a + b/c)/(d - p/q/n)
'B5 brackets around uneven numerator/denominator heights
B_5 = (a/(b/c) + 1)*d
'B6 brackets around a fraction whose denominator is tall
B_6 = (1 + a/(b + c/(d + x)))^2
'B7 chained division
B_7 = a/b/c/d
'B8 fraction next to a power in the numerator
B_8 = (a^2 + b^(1/2))/(c^(d/n))
'<h3>C. Roots</h3>
'C1 root of a fraction
C_1 = sqrt(a/b)
'C2 nested roots
C_2 = sqrt(1 + sqrt(1 + sqrt(x)))
'C3 cube root of a fraction
C_3 = root(a/b; 3)
'C4 root in a denominator
C_4 = 1/sqrt(a^2 + b^2)
'C5 root of a fractional power
C_5 = sqrt(a^(2/3))
'C6 n-th root of a nested fraction
C_6 = root(x/(1 + x/y); 5)
'C7 root raised to a fractional power
C_7 = sqrt(y)^(3/2)
'C8 root of a continued fraction
C_8 = sqrt(1 + 1/(1 + 1/(1 + x)))
'<h3>D. Brackets and absolute value</h3>
'D1 nested bracket levels
D_1 = ((a + b)*(c - (d + (x - y))))^2
'D2 absolute value of a difference of fractions
D_2 = abs(a/b - c/d)
'D3 redundant brackets around a fraction
D_3 = (((a/b)))
'D4 bracketed fraction in a denominator
D_4 = 1/(a/b + c/d)
'<h3>E. Sums, products and integrals</h3>
'E1 sum of a fraction with a power
E_1 = $Sum{1/k^2 @ k = 1 : 10}
'E2 sum in a denominator
E_2 = 1/$Sum{1/k^2 @ k = 1 : 10}
'E3 integral of a fraction
E_3 = $Integral{1/(1 + t^2) @ t = 0 : 1}
'E4 sum with factorial in denominator, over a fraction
E_4 = $Sum{x^k/k! @ k = 0 : 10}/(1 + x)
'E5 product raised to a fractional power
E_5 = $Product{(1 + 1/k^2) @ k = 1 : 10}^(1/2)
'E6 integral with fraction limits
E_6 = $Integral{t^2 @ t = 1/a : a/b}
'<h3>F. Conditionals</h3>
'F1 if with fractions
F_1 = if(a < b; a/b; b/a)
'F2 switch inside a fraction
F_2 = 1/(1 + switch(x < 1; x/2; x < 2; x^2/3; 1))
'<h3>G. Units and number formatting</h3>
'G1 section modulus with units and substitution
G_1 = M/(b_w*h^2/6)|MPa
'G2 unit powers in the denominator
G_2 = q_d/L^2
'G3 fractional unit exponent
G_3 = k_s^2/L
'G4 scientific notation in a denominator
G_4 = 1/(x*10^(-8))
'G5 scientific notation raised to a power
G_5 = (10^(-5))^(1/2)/a
'<h3>H. Subscripts with powers</h3>
'H1 subscripted base with fractional power over subscripted variable
H_1 = sqrt(f_ck/MPa)^(1/2)/γ_c
'H2 subscripts on both sides of a fraction
H_2 = A_1^2/A_3^(2/3)
'H3 subscript and fractional power in a denominator
H_3 = 1/B_1^(n/2)
'<h3>I. Vectors and matrices</h3>
'I1 vector over its norm
v = [1; 2; 3]
I_1 = v/norm(v)
'I2 matrix expression divided by a determinant
K = [a; b|c; d]
I_2 = inverse(K)/det(K)
'<h3>J. Functions</h3>
'J1 squared function of a fraction
J_1 = sin(x/2)^2
'J2 log of a nested fraction
J_2 = ln(1 + x/(y + 1/z))
'J3 function powers in numerator and denominator
J_3 = sin(π/4)^(1/2)/cos(x)^2
'<h3>K. Page-break stress</h3>
'<p>Tall equations in sequence. Print to PDF and check that no equation is split or clipped at a page boundary.</p>
#for i = 1 : 24
K_i = (1 + 1/(1 + 1/(1 + i/x)))^(1/(1 + 1/n))/sqrt(1 + a/(b + c/(d + i)))
#loop
